# Crawl and Apify safety

Do not scrape, crawl, or send to Apify any site that forbids automated access. Doing so can ban the user's LinkedIn / Indeed / Stepstone / ZipRecruiter accounts.

## Hard deny-list (HTTP GET, RSS fetch, Apify start_urls, cookies)

- linkedin.com
- indeed.com (including de.indeed.com)
- stepstone.de / stepstone.com
- ziprecruiter.com
- xing.com
- glassdoor.com / glassdoor.de
- wellfound.com / angel.co

The canonical list lives in `backend/src/jobhunt/policy.py` (`DENIED_CRAWL_HOSTS`). Extend that set; do not special-case a scraper around it.

## Allowed ingest

- Arbeitsagentur Jobsuche API (official-style client, not HTML scrape)
- RSS feeds whose **feed URL** is not on the deny-list
- `_inbox/` Web Clipper notes the **user** already opened (parse the local file only; never fetch the listing URL)
- Public company career / Impressum pages that are **not** on the deny-list, via httpx or a future Apify actor

## Apify

Apify is only for constrained public-page fetches that pass `assert_crawl_allowed`. Never:

- Point an actor at a deny-listed host
- Upload LinkedIn/Indeed cookies or session tokens
- Use Apify to bypass login walls on job boards

If a start URL is denied, **fail the run**. Do not skip silently and crawl anyway.

## Submit

The user submits applications in the browser. No computer-use, no Easy Apply bots.
